```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Background Image Display</title>
    <style>
        body {
            margin: 0;
            height: 100vh;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
        }

        .background-image-container {
            position: relative;
            width: 300px;
            height: 200px;
            overflow: hidden;
        }

        .background-image {
            position: absolute;
            top: 50%;
            left: 50%;
            transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
            z-index: -1; /* Ensure it appears behind other elements */
        }

        #displayImageButton {
            cursor: pointer;
            padding: 10px;
            border: none;
            background-color: #4CAF50;
            color: white;
            text-align: center;
            text-decoration: none;
            display: inline-block;
            font-size: 16px;
            margin-top: 20px;
            transition: background-color 0.3s ease;
        }

        #displayImageButton:hover {
            background-color: #45a049;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <div class="background-image-container">
        <img id="displayImage" src="" alt="Background Image">
    </div>

    <button id="displayImageButton">Show Background Image</button>

<script>
    // Function to get the URL of the current device's background image
    function getImageUrl() {
        const bgImage = document.body.style.backgroundImage.replace(/url\((.*)\)/, '$1');
        return bgImage || 'no_image';
    }

    // Get the image URL from the current device
    let imageUrl = getImageUrl();

    // Set the image source for the display image element
    document.getElementById('displayImage').src = imageUrl;

    // Add event listener to show/hide the image based on button click
    document.getElementById('displayImageButton').addEventListener('click', function () {
        if (document.body.style.backgroundImage === '') {
            document.body.style.backgroundImage = `url(${imageUrl})`;
            this.textContent = "Hide Background Image";
        } else {
            document.body.style.backgroundImage = '';
            this.textContent = "Show Background Image";
        }
    });
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:
1. **HTML Structure**: 
   - The `<div>` with the class `background-image-container` holds an `<img>` tag (`#displayImage`) to display the background image.
   - A `<button>` element with the ID `displayImageButton` triggers the change in the background image.

2. **CSS Styling**:
   - The `.background-image-container` ensures the image fits within the container and hides any scrollbars.
   - The `.background-image` absolutely positions the image at the center of the screen while ensuring it doesn't overlap with the container.

3. **JavaScript Logic**:
   - The `getImageUrl()` function retrieves the current device's background image URL using JavaScript DOM methods.
   - It sets the source of the `<img>` tag in the background image container dynamically.
